WEBVTT

00:25:29.916 --> 00:25:33.464
over to our incoming dean
and our deputy dean,

00:25:33.488 --> 00:25:35.679
who I know is a huge fan of yours,

00:25:35.703 --> 00:25:38.067
and let them know
that when you go up for renewal,

00:25:38.091 --> 00:25:41.423
you would rather be vetted
by an algorithm than by them.

00:25:41.447 --> 00:25:42.598
Are you cool with that?

00:25:42.622 --> 00:25:44.376
CM: (Laughs)

00:25:44.400 --> 00:25:46.201
Sure, I will stand by that.

00:25:46.225 --> 00:25:47.392
AG: Really?

00:25:47.416 --> 00:25:48.575
CM: Yeah, sure, why not?

00:25:48.599 --> 00:25:50.964
Now, do I have any choice
in who builds the model?

00:25:50.988 --> 00:25:52.710
(Laughter)

00:25:52.734 --> 00:25:55.535
AG: Cade's last question
raises a critical point.

00:25:55.559 --> 00:25:57.713
Even algorithms can be biased.

00:25:58.021 --> 00:26:00.822
The calculations may be run by computers,